 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+In supporting browsers, the header exposes `open_search` and `open_reading_list`.
+Opening these panels reveals declarative search and per-article removal forms.
+The article bookmark control also exposes a declarative toggle form. Forms use
+`toolname`, `tooldescription`, `toolautosubmit`, named controls, and
+`SubmitEvent.respondWith()` to return results while updating the visible UI.
+
+Every page also registers `search_articles`, `get_article`, `get_reading_list`,
+`toggle_reading_list`, `get_tide_levels`, `get_coffee_brew`, `get_plant_stats`, and
+`get_article_popularity`. Article identifiers come from search results; popularity
+requires an `id`. Toggle operations remove an existing bookmark or add a missing
+one. Reading lists use the existing browser session. The four article API tools
+return HTTP status, redirect information, and response data, preserving the demo
+APIs' intentional failures.
+
+Registration uses feature-detected `document.modelContext` (with an early-browser
+`navigator.modelContext` fallback), and cleans up on component unmount and Astro
+navigation. Browsers without WebMCP retain the normal controls.
+See the [WebMCP specification](https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp) and
+[declarative API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
+
+Run non-browser lifecycle and form-response tests with `node --test tests/webmcp.test.mjs`
+(Node 24 or another runtime with TypeScript type stripping).
